          <msContents>
            <summary>An essay on Man based on Genesis II, 7-the Creation of Man-and written on theosophical principles, the doctrine of Microcosm and Macrocosm, etc.
              Das ist: Vom Erkentnis sein selbst von der Mensch seinen Ursprung, Wandel und Ende erkennen soll beides nach der Natur und nach der Gnaden. 
              It is perhaps the work of a follower of Paracelsus, who is referred to in the later chapters. [Cf. Sudhoff 'Versuch', Vol. II, pp. 636, 637 for an unpublished MS. 'Super nosce te ipsum'.].
              This manuscript contains a portion of the Book of Esther.
            </summary>
            <textLang mainLang="de" source="IANA">German</textLang>
